  "worked_solution": "Let's add $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ to the plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254493/assets/2ae4b6366911ec501f39eec2461e7a392526f103e25f9471391932a64a23513a.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, shift it by $5$ units **up**.\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+5.$",
